    "question": "A damped oscillator of mass $m = 0.60\\text{ kg}$ has spring constant $k = 55.0\\text{ N m}^{-1}$ and damping coefficient $b = 0.06\\text{ kg s}^{-1}$. What is its quality factor $Q$?",
    "options": {
      "A": "95.7",
      "B": "191.5",
      "C": "47.9",
      "D": "143.6"
    },
    "optionsList": [
      "95.7",
      "191.5",
      "47.9",
      "143.6"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "$\\omega_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{55.0}{0.60}} \\approx 9.57\\text{ rad s}^{-1}$. Quality factor $Q = \\frac{\\omega_0 m}{b} = \\frac{9.57 \\times 0.60}{0.06} \\approx 95.7$.",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "subject": "Physics",
    "class": "11",
    "chapter": "oscillations",
    "topicId": "phys-resonance-damped",
    "subtopic": "Quality Factor Multi-parameter Calculation",
